package log

// Trusted minimal stub of stdlib `log` for Gobra verification.
// Used by clock.SetNow's backwards-motion warning (Stream 2 Phase 0):
// `log.Printf` emits a warning when an admin snapshot tries to set the
// clock backwards (F7 forbids it). Gobra needs a declaration of the
// symbol to type-check the import.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stream 3 Phase 6 retirement investigation (2026-05-03)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Investigated whether Gobra's bundled stdlib (inside the docker image
// `ghcr.io/viperproject/gobra@sha256:2ef080ccd284945829501996e6d63ed2f1c94b7cf6a30d2b934272fb8a6df2c6`,
// pinned in .github/workflows/verify.yml) ships a usable `log` spec we
// could import in lieu of this shim.
//
// Findings: NO. The bundled stubs inside `gobra.jar` are limited to:
//   builtin/builtin.gobra
//   stubs/bytes/bytes.gobra
//   stubs/encoding/binary/binary.gobra
//   stubs/errors/wrap.gobra
//   stubs/fmt/fmt.gobra            <- placeholder only ("no members supported")
//   stubs/net/{ip,iprawsock,net,udpsock}.gobra
//   stubs/strconv/{atoi,itoa}.gobra
//   stubs/strings/strings.gobra
//   stubs/sync/{mutex,waitgroup}.gobra
//   stubs/time/{sleep,time,zoneinfo}.gobra
// There is no `stubs/log/*.gobra`, and even fmt is just a package-stub
// with no exported members (so Printf/Println would not be visible from
// any "import this and inherit specs" path even by analogy). Verified by
// extracting gobra.jar and listing entries: `unzip -l gobra.jar | grep .gobra`.
//
// Decision: KEEP this shim. It is the minimal possible TCB cost — two
// `// @ trusted` declarations of side-effect-free I/O wrappers that the
// verifier never reasons about beyond their type signature. There is no
// safer upstream artifact to substitute. Re-evaluate if/when Gobra adds
// a bundled `log` stub or when the project decides to drop the warning
// log line from clock.SetNow entirely.

// @ trusted
// @ decreases _
func Printf(format string, v ...interface{})

// @ trusted
// @ decreases _
func Println(v ...interface{})
